{"step_index":531,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T16:54:54Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-08-23T16:54:54Z sender=81f4039b-1209-4116-aaf0-2512c0fe7280 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=Here is the analysis of the README.md files for each of the 13 requested repositories located in `C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\find-skill-repo\\all github repos`:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **ruflo**\n- **Summary:** Ruflo is an agent meta-harness and execution layer for Claude Code and Codex that coordinates 100+ specialized agents, swarms, and persistent vector memory (AgentDB/HNSW). It automates multi-agent collaboration, background workers, and zero-trust cross-machine agent federation without manual orchestration.\n- **Requires GPU:** **No** (Runs on CPU as a Node.js/Rust orchestration harness; optional GPU acceleration is available if routing to local models via Ollama/vLLM or RuVector GPU search).\n- **Minimum RAM:** **~512 MB – 2 GB RAM** (standard developer environment).\n\n---\n\n### 2. **unsloth**\n- **Summary:** Unsloth is a high-performance LLM training, fine-tuning, and inference platform available as both a web interface (Unsloth Studio) and a Python library (Unsloth Core). It accelerates model training up to 2x–12x while cutting VRAM usage by 70%–80% across 500+ text, vision, audio, and embedding models.\n- **Requires GPU:** **Yes** for model training and full GPU acceleration (NVIDIA RTX/Blackwell, AMD ROCm, Intel Arc, or Apple Silicon via MLX), though CPU is supported for basic chat/data recipes and GGUF inference mode.\n- **Minimum RAM:** **~6 GB – 8 GB VRAM** for fine-tuning smaller models (16 GB – 24 GB+ VRAM for larger models); **~8 GB – 16 GB system RAM** for CPU execution.\n\n---\n\n### 3. **comfyui**\n- **Summary:** ComfyUI is a modular, node/graph-based visual AI creation engine for designing and executing generative workflows across image, video, audio, and 3D models. It offers granular pipeline control for architectures like Stab\n<truncated 4564 bytes>\nsues when searching for agent skills on Windows. It updates the skill instructions to execute search and discovery commands via PowerShell rather than standard Git Bash.\n- **Requires GPU:** **No** (Markdown configuration and lightweight Node.js/PowerShell commands).\n- **Minimum RAM:** **<512 MB system RAM**.\n\n---\n\n### 11. **gstack**\n- **Summary:** gstack is an open-source suite of skills and structured workflow roles for Claude Code and other AI coding agents that simulate a full virtual engineering team. It provides specialized slash commands for product brainstorming, CEO/eng/design reviews, browser-based QA automation, security auditing, and release engineering.\n- **Requires GPU:** **No** (runs on CPU as Markdown prompt definitions, Bash/TypeScript scripts, and Bun/Node CLI tools).\n- **Minimum RAM:** **~512 MB – 2 GB system RAM**.\n\n---\n\n### 12. **handy**\n- **Summary:** Handy is a free, open-source cross-platform desktop application built with Tauri (Rust + React) that provides private, offline speech-to-text transcription. It allows users to press a global shortcut, transcribe speech locally using Whisper or CPU-optimized Parakeet V3 models with Silero VAD, and directly paste text into active applications.\n- **Requires GPU:** **No** (runs efficiently on CPU using Parakeet V3 or CPU Whisper via GGML/GGUF, with optional GPU acceleration supported).\n- **Minimum RAM:** **~1 GB – 4 GB system RAM** (depending on the selected Whisper or Parakeet model size).\n\n---\n\n### 13. **agent-browser**\n- **Summary:** agent-browser is a fast native Rust CLI and daemon designed for AI agents to automate and interact with web browsers via accessibility tree snapshots and refs. It enables AI assistants to open pages, click/fill elements, take annotated screenshots, execute JavaScript, and stream browser sessions with minimal token overhead.\n- **Requires GPU:** **No** (runs on CPU using headless Chrome/Chromium automation).\n- **Minimum RAM:** **~1 GB – 2 GB system RAM** for headless Chrome and daemon operation.\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>","truncated_fields":["content"]}
