{"step_index":535,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T16:55:09Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-08-23T16:55:07Z sender=aea5b86b-03b5-4625-a09c-95c79e069ecb priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=Here is the summary, GPU requirements, and minimum RAM specifications for the 12 requested repositories in `C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\find-skill-repo\\all github repos`:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **remotion-main**\n* **Summary:** Remotion is a React-based programmatic video creation and animation framework that allows developers and coding agents to build videos using standard web technologies. It supports programmatic composition, interactive editing, design systems, and scalable batch rendering on local or cloud infrastructure.\n* **GPU Required:** **No** (Runs on CPU via Node.js and headless Chromium; hardware acceleration is optional).\n* **Minimum RAM:** **2 GB – 4 GB** (Baseline memory required for Node.js and headless browser rendering).\n\n---\n\n### 2. **remotion-motion-graphics-skill-main**\n* **Summary:** This repository provides a suite of Agent Skills that teach AI coding agents to create broadcast-quality motion graphics and visual assets using Remotion. It enforces structured production gates, continuous camera choreographies, authentic terminal demos, and editorial highlight cards without human keyframing.\n* **GPU Required:** **No** (Executes via Remotion on CPU).\n* **Minimum RAM:** **2 GB – 4 GB** (Standard Remotion / Node.js execution footprint).\n\n---\n\n### 3. **video-shotcraft-main**\n* **Summary:** video-shotcraft is an AI agent skill that transforms coding assistants into motion-design studios for creating cinematic product promos and demo videos with Remotion. It includes 152 shot recipe cards, 209 motion styles/previews, sound design passes, and an Ink Press promo template with CapCut/JianYing draft export support.\n* **GPU Required:** **No** (Tested on headless 2-core CPU environments using Remotion).\n* **Minimum RAM:** **2 GB – 4\n<truncated 3329 bytes>\ntware engineering, design, marketing, product, and strategy tasks. It can be installed into AI coding tools (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI, Antigravity) to provide dedicated domain experts with proven deliverables.\n* **GPU Required:** **No** (Collection of markdown prompt files and shell integration scripts).\n* **Minimum RAM:** **Minimal (< 512 MB)** (Negligible storage/memory requirement as it contains markdown instruction files).\n\n---\n\n### 10. **superpowers**\n* **Summary:** Superpowers is a software development methodology and composable skill framework for AI coding agents that enforces structured scoping, test-driven development (TDD), and subagent orchestration. It prevents AI assistants from hallucinating or drifting by breaking work into verifiable, testable steps before writing code.\n* **GPU Required:** **No** (Markdown instructions and skills for AI agent harnesses).\n* **Minimum RAM:** **Minimal (< 512 MB)** (Text/instruction files only).\n\n---\n\n### 11. **last30days-skill-main**\n* **Summary:** /last30days is an AI agent research skill and search engine that queries real-time sentiment and engagement across Reddit, X, YouTube, TikTok, Hacker News, Polymarket, and GitHub. It synthesizes multi-platform data, top community comments, and engagement metrics into a concise brief covering recent events.\n* **GPU Required:** **No** (Lightweight Python/Node scripts, API integrations, and web scrapers).\n* **Minimum RAM:** **1 GB – 2 GB** (Standard lightweight CLI/scripting environment).\n\n---\n\n### 12. **marketingskills**\n* **Summary:** Marketing Skills is a repository of specialized AI agent skills covering conversion rate optimization (CRO), copywriting, SEO, paid advertising, and growth marketing. It equips AI coding agents with battle-tested frameworks, interrelated context trees, and best practices across the marketing lifecycle.\n* **GPU Required:** **No** (Collection of markdown skill definition documents).\n* **Minimum RAM:** **Minimal (< 512 MB)** (Instructional markdown files only).\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":536,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T16:55:09Z","content":"Both agents are done. Let me now compile the full audit.","thinking":"Both audit groups have responded. Now I have the full picture. Let me compile the audit of what Gemini said vs what the actual READMEs say, and identify what was correct, what was wrong, and give final recommendations.\n\nLet me cross-reference:\n\n**Gemini's previous claims vs. Audit findings:**\n\n1. **ruflo (1.76 GB)** - Gemini said: \"❌ Delete - heavy framework, likely downloaded heavy local models, needs GPU.\" Audit says: NO GPU required, runs on CPU as Node.js/Rust orchestration, ~512MB-2GB RAM. **GEMINI WAS WRONG.** Ruflo doesn't need a GPU at all. \n\nIt's just an orchestration harness, though 1.76 GB still seems like a lot for a coordination tool.\n\n2. **unsloth (62 MB)** - Gemini said it needs a dedicated GPU for training AI models, and the audit confirms this is correct, requiring 6-8GB VRAM minimum for fine-tuning.\n\n3. **comfyui (43 MB)** - Gemini said it needs a GPU for AI image generation, and the audit confirms GPU is practically required here too.\n\n4. Checking speech-to-text next, Gemini claimed it needs a dedicated GPU, but the audit shows CPU fallbacks exist even though GPU is strongly recommended for real-time use, so Gemini was only partially right since it can run on CPU but slowly.\n\n5. **OmniVoice (1.26 MB)** - Gemini flagged it as needing a dedicated GPU, and the audit mostly agrees GPU is strongly recommended even though CPU execution is technically supported.\n\n6. **ViMax (3.14 MB)** - Gemini said it needs a dedicated GPU, but the audit shows it actually requires no GPU at all, relying on cloud APIs with just 4-8GB RAM, so Gemini got this one wrong.\n\nMoving through the rest of the list, I'm confirming Gemini was correct about MoneyPrinterTurbo, OpenReels, and OpenMontage all working fine on a laptop via cloud APIs with no GPU needed, and now I'm checking HyperFrames next.\n\nConfirming that deletion was right since npx handles everything. I also notice several small repos Gemini never analyzed at all—graphify, Pixelle-Video, Scrapling, findskill, gstack, handy, agent-browser, and remotion-motion-graphics-skill-main—all lightweight tools with no GPU requirements that were simply skipped in the original review.\n\nContinuing through the smaller skills: YouTube automation, NotebookLM tool, book-to-skill converter, MCP reference, social media skills, text humanizer, ad prompt guide, thumbnail tools, and an anti-AI-writing skill called stop-slop.\n\nI also spot visual-skills, plus Agent-Reach appearing twice as duplicates for browser interaction. Checking the video tools more carefully, MoneyPrinterTurbo, OpenReels, and OpenMontage aren't truly identical despite Gemini's claim -- they target short videos, vertical shorts, and general agentic video production respectively, though similar enough for the user's needs. I also notice Gemini missed mentioning remotion-motion-graphics-skill and video-shotcraft entirely, which are Remotion-based skills.\n\nNow I'm confirming the duplicate pairs: Agent-Reach and Agent-Reach-main, plus super-video-maker-skill and super-video-maker-skill-main, before moving on to write the full audit artifact.","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Full audit and fact-check of Gemini's previous analysis of 43 GitHub repos in the user's find-skill-repo folder. Identifies 3 incorrect claims (ruflo, ViMax, speech-to-speech wrongly flagged as needing GPU), confirms 10 correct claims, documents 25+ repos Gemini skipped entirely, finds 2 duplicate repo pairs, and provides final delete/keep recommendations tailored to the user's Intel i5 / 8GB RAM / Intel Iris Xe laptop.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# 🔍 Full Audit: Gemini's GitHub Repo Analysis\\n\\nI re-read every single README across all 43 repos using independent auditors. Here is the fact-check of what Gemini told you, what it got wrong, and my final recommendation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ❌ Where Gemini Was WRONG\\n\\n### 1. **ruflo** (1.76 GB) — Gemini said \\\"Delete, needs GPU\\\"\\n> **WRONG.** Ruflo does NOT need a GPU at all. It's a lightweight Node.js/Rust orchestration tool that coordinates AI agents. It runs fine on CPU with ~512 MB RAM. However, 1.76 GB is bloated for what it does — the `.git` history and `node_modules` are likely inflated. **Verdict: It CAN run on your laptop, but 1.76 GB is excessive for a coordination tool. You can reinstall it smaller if you ever need it.**\\n\\n### 2. **ViMax** (3.14 MB) — Gemini said \\\"Delete, needs GPU\\\"\\n> **WRONG.** ViMax does NOT need a GPU. It's a Python orchestration tool that sends all heavy work (video generation, scripts, storyboarding) to cloud APIs (OpenAI, Gemini, Veo, Kling). It needs only 4–8 GB RAM. **Verdict: This RUNS FINE on your laptop. Gemini incorrectly lumped it with GPU-heavy tools.**\\n\\n### 3. **speech-to-speech** (2.83 MB) — Gemini said \\\"Delete, needs GPU\\\"\\n> **PARTIALLY WRONG.** It has CPU fallback modes and can work using cloud APIs for the LLM and TTS parts. A GPU is only \\\"strongly recommended\\\" for real-time low-latency voice chat. For basic use, your laptop can handle it. **Verdict: Usable on your laptop, just not for real-time live voice conversations.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ✅ Where Gemini Was CORRECT\\n\\n| Repo | Gemini Said | Audit Confirms |\\n|:-----|:-----------|:---------------|\\n| **unsloth** (62 MB) | ❌ Delete, needs GPU | ✅ Correct — needs 6–8 GB VRAM minimum |\\n| **comfyui** (43 MB) | ❌ Delete, needs GPU | ✅ Correct — GPU practically required |\\n| **OmniVoice** (1.26 MB) | ❌ Delete, needs GPU | ✅ Correct — GPU strongly recommended |\\n| **MoneyPrinterTurbo** (200 MB) | ✅ Keep, cloud APIs | ✅ Correct — no GPU, 4 GB RAM minimum |\\n| **OpenReels** (64 M\n<truncated 5271 bytes>","Description":"\"Complete fact-check audit of Gemini's repo analysis — verifying every claim against actual READMEs, catching errors, identifying missed repos, and providing final recommendations.\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\b75d3ef6-c7ea-497e-a92f-fe05edd5e5c3\\\\repo_audit.md\"","toolAction":"\"Write audit artifact\"","toolSummary":"\"Repo audit report\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
